  "body_text": "96 \r\n🥾 Plus: Rock towers | Thursday, August 13, 2026\r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n View in browser \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n Axios Finish Line By\r\nMike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei\r\n &middot; Aug 13, 2026 \r\nAug 13, 2026\r\n \r\n \r\n 🎣 Finish Line is goin' fishing for two weeks after tonight's edition, and we'll see you Aug. 31st. Until then, soak up your summer finale!\n\n ✨ Happy Thursday! Smart Brevity™ count: 351 words … 1½ mins. Edited by Amy Stern. \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n1 big thing: The grandparent advantage\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Stock: Getty Images\n\n\r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n The gift of grandparenthood offers the chance to help raise a child, pass on traditions and get more fit chasing a toddler around.\n\n 👵 Research suggests the role may also be linked to healthier aging and, in some cases, a longer life. ⏳ The big picture: Grandparents who hit the sweet spot of involvement — not overextending, but being present and supportive — can experience physical, cognitive and emotional benefits, Axios' Natalie Daher writes. \n\n Geriatric psychiatrist Marc Agronin recently outlined some of those benefits in The Wall Street Journal ( gift link ):\n\n 1. 💪 It requires a can-do spirit: Children come with activities, schedules and the need for an adult in the room as they learn how to navigate the world, including sibling squabbles. \n\n Stepping up for these tasks can help build a grandparent's sense of competence and usefulness, and in turn a more positive view of aging. Yale psychologist Becca Levy has found that people with positive beliefs about aging lived, on average, 7½ years longer. 2. ❤️ It provides purpose: Grandparenting offers another vantage point on parenting — and, sometimes, a chance to do things differently from the first go-round.\n\n Cooking family recipes with a new, younger partner in crime, for example, offers an opportunity to pass on wisdom and history. 3. 👟 You gotta keep up: Grandparenting can lead to plenty of physical activity when you're trying to match the energy of a kid. \n\n One study Agronin highlights found that moderate involvement in caring for grandchildren was associated with fewer mobility limitations, fewer depressive symptoms and better cognition, compared with no involvement. 💞 The bottom line: The bond between grandparents and grandchildren is special and lasting — and benefits three generations.\n\n\r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n &nbsp; \r\nA message from Axios\r\n\n\r\n \r\n Don't Miss: Our Quarterly Report on Ad Economics \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Media Trends Executive just released its exclusive quarterly report on the forces reshaping ad economics.\n\n\r\n \r\n Built for executives, it pairs expert reporting with essential data and charts to show where ad dollars are moving next. \r\n \r\n 🔒 Become a member today to unlock this exclusive Media Trends Executive report.\n\n\r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n2. 🏜️ Parting shot: Into the maze\r\n \r\n \r\n Photo: Bill Pearson Reader Bill Pearson of Philadelphia captured this view along White Rim Road in Canyonlands National Park in Utah last year. \n\n It's his favorite for its surreal landscape and maze of canyons. \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n 🏁 Please invite your friends to join Finish Line . \n\n\r\n \r\n 👆 Like this comms style and format? It's called Smart Brevity®. Bring it to your org — via hands-on training or internal comms software — to harness its power and impact. \r\n \r\n &nbsp; Axios thanks our partners for supporting our journalism.\n Advertise with us. \n\n Read more about Axios' mission , ethics and how we use AI in our journalism . You can reach the authors by replying to this email.\nSponsorship has no influence on editorial content.\n\n Thank you for signing up for this Axios newsletter. To stop receiving this newsletter, unsubscribe or manage your email preferences . If someone forwarded this to you, sign up now to get Axios in your inbox.\n\n Axios, PO Box 101060, Arlington VA 22201 &nbsp; Follow Axios across:\n\n &nbsp; &nbsp; \r\n \r\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;",
